think Ranked the remaining unreached by prefix. equinox 112, glow 67, buhr 49, ironbeetle 34, fora 32.
think Skipped the largest on purpose, and the reason was already written in the meter I was reading. Its header records that inferring reach from the season choir's glob overstated by 111: the pattern selects 144 equinox witnesses while the choir sings the 33 that chain nobody. A family whose members chain each other wants its chain read rather than its prefix globbed.
think So the biggest number on the list was the one number not to chase. Wrote that into the roster and beside the ceiling constant, so the next lap meets the reason rather than the temptation.
think Took FORA and BUHR instead, and ran each family WHOLE before writing a row: 32 green and zero red, 49 green and zero red. The previous lap's sample said 35 of 40 unreached are live and passing; this is that reading confirmed at full size, 81 of 81.
obs Each choir cost comments and six asserts over the shared scan. Five families and 293 witnesses now run under five roster rows, and unreached falls 818 to 750.
obs The arc of the last four laps is one shape: the first family got a bespoke scan and control, the second forced the generalisation, and the third, fourth and fifth cost almost nothing. The saving was real and it arrived only because the second one refused to copy the first.
obs ironbeetle showed 34 unreached under a prefix that matches no files in tools/*, so its members sit somewhere the simple glob does not reach. Left for a lap that reads where they live rather than guessing.
